  "issue_title": "Review source roles for 33 Alaska ecoregion fragments",
  "issue_body": "Parent: #486. This is a bounded, source-only follow-up from the Western North America interior batch 2 audit. It is blocked until #486 is merged and remains under regional integration #484.\n\nAudit finding: all 33 assigned Alaska physical fragments in #486 derive from RESOLVE ecoregion features, but their retained metadata says `source_role=Counties` and source selection rationale references counties. See parent packet `data/regional-review/regional-review-93f8f3bee8e205be/derived-portion-audit.json` and `assessment.json`. The 33 exact fragment IDs and Eco_IDs are listed there. Seven underlying geoBoundaries USA ADM2 2018 county predecessors each split into RESOLVE ecological pieces. RESOLVE item 37ea320eebb647c6838c23f72abae5ef2 is licensed CC BY 4.0; its 2017 ecoregion classification is not administrative geography.\n\nDeliver a source/role correction recommendation for these 33 IDs, documenting source lineage, role/tier/license and preserved parent membership. Do not edit shared hierarchy or geometry; location membership determines parent footprints. Create evidence and coordinate integration with #484.\n\n<!-- worldatlas-work:v1\n{\"max_prs\":1,\"depends_on\":[486],\"scope\":\"Bounded role/provenance review for exactly 33 Alaska RESOLVE ecoregion fragment IDs itemized in #486 evidence; recommendations only\",\"mode\":\"geography\",\"owned_paths\":[\"data/regional-review/alaska-ecoregion-role-followup-2026/\"]}\n-->\n",
